# Content, SEO & quality

## Content

- Original, useful writing for real players (all levels). No thin/spun filler or keyword stuffing.
- Reference only products that exist in `gear.json`.
- Articles: clear H1, hierarchical H2/H3, fast-answer intro, comparison tables when useful, FAQ (FAQPage schema), pros/cons, ≥3 internal links + link to the relevant category page.
- Hero images (guides + news): use **`heroImage`/`image` + `heroAlt`/`imageAlt`**. Source only from **Unsplash, Pexels, Pixabay, or Wikimedia Commons** (keep CC credit fields). Never reuse random search results from news sites, blogs, or brand marketing pages.
- **News heroes are required and must be in the repo.** Download to `public/images/news/` and point `image` at `/images/news/…`. Never ship Wikimedia `Special:FilePath` hotlinks. No photographer watermarks. Run `npm run qa:news` (also runs before `npm run build`). Guides may still hotlink Unsplash CDNs.

## SEO

- Every page: unique title (≤60), meta description (≤155), canonical, OG + Twitter with per-page image.
- JSON-LD: Article on articles; Product/Review where applicable; FAQPage; BreadcrumbList; site-wide Organization.
- Keep internal linking strong; confirm sitemap includes new routes after build.

## Quality gates

- Run `npm run build` after every meaningful change. Never commit a red build.
- Semantic HTML, alt text on all images, WCAG AA contrast, keyboard navigable.
- Prefer Astro `<Image>` with explicit width/height; lazy-load below the fold.
- Mobile-first; comparison tables must degrade on small screens.

## Commits

- Small, focused conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`.
- List any new `{{ TODO: confirm }}` items in the summary.
